{"type":"text","timestamp":1794229856952,"sessionID":"ses_e3f92f8eeffe09UHSluY4LVAFN","part":{"id":"prt_1c06eda42001iNNXBnhUq1yF4a","sessionID":"ses_e3f92f8eeffe09UHSluY4LVAFN","messageID":"msg_1c06e89fa001Hq0EOaXyk9X17p","type":"text","text":"<answer>\nTo use the `list_mcp_resources` tool from the `opencode` namespace, you would structure the call as follows:\n\n```typescript\nawait tools.opencode.list_mcp_resources({\n  server: \"exampleServer\" // Optional: specify the MCP server name\n});\n```\n\nThis retrieves documents, records, and data from the specified MCP server. The result includes `resources` (direct data) and `templates` (URI templates for dynamic data access). Use this when the user refers to external data sources managed by MCP servers.\n\nFor example, if the user asks, \"What datasets are available on the 'exampleServer'?\" this tool would provide the list of resources and templates to interact with them.\n</answer>","time":{"start":1794229852738,"end":1794229856952}}}
